{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q018_tal_effector_repeat_lengths","answer":"All three domains are classified in family a.298.1.1 (TAL (transcription activator-like) effector) in SCOPe 2.08, under superfamily a.298.1 (TAL effector-like) and fold a.298 (Left-handed alpha-alpha superhelix). The family is defined by a shared tandem-repeat architecture rather than by a single compact globular domain, so the classification is at the level of the repeat unit. Different sequence lengths are expected because the domains differ in how many repeat units they contain (copy number), while each repeat shares the same left-handed alpha-helical hairpin organization. The length difference therefore does not argue against family membership; it reflects a repeat-count difference.

The SCOPe annotations support this reading. d2kq5a_ (PDB 2kq5 chain A, protein PthA, Xanthomonas axonopodis pv. citri) carries the comment "single repeat", so it represents one repeat unit rather than a full array. d4cj9a_ (4cj9 chain A, protein BurrH, Burkholderia rhizoxinica) has a repeat annotation of 4cj9 A:259-292, a 34-residue canonical repeat, and its comment notes it is complexed with a second ligand, but the repeat coordinates apply to the requested node. d3v6pa_ (3v6p chain A, protein dHax3, Xanthomonas) has no comment. Family-level "re" inconsistency flags on d2kq5a_ and d3v6pa_ state that the family's common domain can be composed of a different number of small repeating units, which is the explicit SCOPe acknowledgement of this length variation.

Limits: (1) I did not retrieve sequence lengths or repeat counts for the three domains, so the specific number of repeats in each and the exact length difference are unverified here; the explanation rests on the SCOPe annotations, not on measured lengths. (2) The 4cj9 A:259-292 coordinates are a canonical-representative repeat for the family and must not be transferred as exact boundaries to d2kq5a_ or d3v6pa_. (3) Shared family membership is curated homology at the family level for repeat architecture; it does not establish function, DNA-binding specificity, or sequence-level identity between the three proteins, and the protein-level differences (PthA, dHax3, BurrH) are below the family level. (4) Any new target matched only by structure or sequence should be treated as a candidate relationship, not as an official a.298.1.1 assignment, without a repeat-aware structural or sequence analysis.","evidence_used":["mcp__scope__get_scop_domains (d2kq5a_, d3v6pa_, d4cj9a_; includes parents, annotations)","mcp__scope__get_scop_node (a.298.1.1, kind sccs, includes parents)","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/a.298.1.1","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/a.298.1.1/parents"]}]}
